# What Vercel must not upload.
#
# `excludeFiles` in vercel.json trims the FUNCTION BUNDLE; it does not trim the upload.
# The first deploy attempt pushed 864 MB and was rejected for a single file over 100 MB,
# because this repo legitimately carries things a serverless function has no use for: a
# vendored 339 MB CockroachDB binary, a local virtualenv, and a Terraform provider that
# is larger than both. None of it is needed to serve the demo.
#
# Everything excluded here is either reproducible (venv, caches), a local-only tool
# (cockroach binary, cluster data), or a deployment artifact for a DIFFERENT target
# (Terraform providers, the Lambda build). The application itself is axiom/ + web/ +
# main.py + certs/, which is a few hundred kilobytes.

# local toolchain and data
.venv/
.local-crdb/
cockroach-v*/
cockroach-data/
*.tgz

# runtime dumps from a local single-node cluster
heap_profiler/
pprof_dump/
goroutine_dump/
inflight_trace_dump/
executiontrace_dump/
preflight.log

# other deployment targets — none of this runs on Vercel
deploy/terraform/.terraform/
deploy/terraform/
deploy/lambda/build/
deploy/lambda/*.zip
deploy/free-tier/
deploy/ecs/

# not needed to serve a request
tests/
docs/
scripts/
skills/
.github/

# caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
